              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Department of Justice), according to Petitioner (Department of Justice), according to Petitioner (Department of Justice), congress directed the Veterans Court to consider the rule of prejudicial error when reviewing administrative determinations of veterans benefits."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner (Department of Justice)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Department of Justice), according to Petitioner (Department of Justice), according to Petitioner (Department of Justice), the burden of showing prejudice from an error lies with the challenger, a principle known to Congress and cited by the Ninth Circuit."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner (Department of Justice)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 15,
                "start": 15
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Department of Justice), according to Petitioner (Department of Justice), according to Petitioner (Department of Justice), the error was not prejudicial because the veteran could only receive increased benefits if the hearing showed a worsening condition."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Christopher J. Meade",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christopher J. Meade, notice is integral to the system designed by Congress; a failure to provide notice is likely to prejudice the veteran."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Christopher J. Meade",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
